  m_text: "Van Gogh made more than twenty self-portraits in his two years in Paris
    (1886\u20131888). With a mirror instead of a model, he tried out the bright colours
    and short, broken strokes he saw in the Impressionists' paintings.\n\nLook closer:
    the background is made of short dashes of blue and orange, and the same colours
    come back in his face and beard.\n\nHold B to ask him a question.\n\nCollection:
    The Art Institute of Chicago (1954.326)"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3b3e2ed9b7e13493988c908d708aead2, type: 2}
